00:00:00.709 --> 00:00:01.796
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.796 --> 00:00:03.521
today's message is just do it.

00:00:03.521 --> 00:00:05.713
Over to you, J.J. Abrhams.

00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:08.057
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.057 --> 00:00:11.190
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.538
♫ Entspresso keep be going

00:00:13.538 --> 00:00:17.474
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.474 --> 00:00:22.295
- Because the resources have
been so limited for so long,

00:00:22.295 --> 00:00:23.997
there are a lot of people who would say,

00:00:23.997 --> 00:00:25.613
god, if I only had

00:00:25.613 --> 00:00:27.194
access to a camera I would make a movie.

00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:28.593
There's a lot of talk about it.

00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:29.837
I remember when I was in college,

00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:33.664
I spent most of my time in
my room writing screenplays.

00:00:33.664 --> 00:00:38.611
Really bad screenplays, but
I was in my room doing that,

00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:42.841
when I probably should have
been studying or something.

00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:44.883
There are a lot of people
I remember at parties

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:46.189
who would talk about writing

00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:47.425
and that they want to be a writer.

00:00:47.425 --> 00:00:48.894
But I would also notice that they were out

00:00:48.894 --> 00:00:50.087
every time I happened to go out,

00:00:50.087 --> 00:00:51.284
they would always be out

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.027
and I just know that their
people who talk about

00:00:54.027 --> 00:00:55.330
what they'd do if,

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.226
but they're not actually doing anything.

00:00:57.226 --> 00:00:58.984
And so, it's a lot easier actually,

00:00:58.984 --> 00:01:00.434
to write a screenplay
than you think it is.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.554
Might not be good,

00:01:01.554 --> 00:01:04.500
but most people talk
about writing screenplays

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.928
but don't actually write them.

00:01:05.928 --> 00:01:07.023
The people who write them,

00:01:07.023 --> 00:01:08.739
you're already like in the top 10%,

00:01:08.739 --> 00:01:10.187
because you've actually written it.

00:01:10.187 --> 00:01:11.404
- To achieve your goal in business,

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:14.153
you need to think big and start small.

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:16.018
To achieve your goal in business,

00:01:16.018 --> 00:01:19.231
you need to think big and start small.

00:01:19.231 --> 00:01:21.981
Be the CEO and the janitor, both.

00:01:23.159 --> 00:01:25.652
Too many entrepreneurs
just want to be the CEO,

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.145
just want to be the visionary,

00:01:27.145 --> 00:01:28.704
just want to come up with all the ideas.

00:01:28.704 --> 00:01:30.134
But you don't want to do any of the work

00:01:30.134 --> 00:01:31.374
and you need both.

00:01:31.374 --> 00:01:33.169
You need the vision,
you need the guidance,

00:01:33.169 --> 00:01:34.861
you need the high level thinking,

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.602
but you need to do the work.

00:01:37.602 --> 00:01:40.056
The janitor does the work.

00:01:40.056 --> 00:01:42.345
And that's what so many
entrepreneurs are missing.

00:01:42.345 --> 00:01:44.516
You just want to play in the big picture,

00:01:44.516 --> 00:01:46.927
but you don't actually
want to get anything done.

00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:47.973
And if that's you,

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:51.153
then your ideas going to die with you.

00:01:51.153 --> 00:01:54.153
You're going to die this
really bitter old person,

00:01:54.153 --> 00:01:57.049
who always had these big visionary ideas,

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:59.720
but never had the team to do it.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.015
Never had the resources to do it.

00:02:01.015 --> 00:02:02.334
Never had the support to do it

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.748
and whatever excuse you
want to throw out there.

00:02:04.748 --> 00:02:06.139
But really, it's because you didn't want

00:02:06.139 --> 00:02:07.673
to get down in the trenches

00:02:07.673 --> 00:02:09.154
and clean the toilet.

00:02:09.154 --> 00:02:11.532
You didn't want to do the grungy, grimey,

00:02:11.532 --> 00:02:13.447
hustle daily, in and out work.

00:02:13.447 --> 00:02:17.196
And at the start, you need to do the work.

00:02:17.196 --> 00:02:18.881
Like, yes, as you get up,

00:02:18.881 --> 00:02:20.944
as you build a team,

00:02:20.944 --> 00:02:22.228
as you start having success,

00:02:22.228 --> 00:02:24.137
you can move higher
and higher up the chain

00:02:24.137 --> 00:02:26.437
and just be more of that visionary.

00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:28.081
But at the start, when it's just you,

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.646
you got to do everything.

00:02:29.646 --> 00:02:30.810
You got to hustle it out.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:32.969
If I look at this YouTube channel,

00:02:32.969 --> 00:02:35.280
I started doing everything.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.687
In my first video,

00:02:36.687 --> 00:02:38.556
I collabed with a friend of mine,

00:02:38.556 --> 00:02:39.907
he helped me film it,

00:02:39.907 --> 00:02:43.574
but most of my videos
at the start, were me.

00:02:44.682 --> 00:02:48.827
Me with a camera, with no
lighting and no microphone

00:02:48.827 --> 00:02:50.183
and sometimes it was wobbly

00:02:50.183 --> 00:02:51.707
and the focus was out

00:02:51.707 --> 00:02:53.584
and it was hard to see me.

00:02:53.584 --> 00:02:55.319
Me doing the editing,

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:59.236
which was Windows Movie
Maker at the beginning.

00:03:00.316 --> 00:03:02.818
Very basic, very simple, very plain.

00:03:02.818 --> 00:03:04.110
Me doing the naming,

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.155
me doing the tagging,

00:03:05.155 --> 00:03:06.348
me doing the promotion,

00:03:06.348 --> 00:03:07.456
me doing the background research,

00:03:07.456 --> 00:03:10.352
me doing the in front of the camera stuff,

00:03:10.352 --> 00:03:11.792
me doing the audio recording.

00:03:11.792 --> 00:03:13.243
Everything, me, it was
me, I did everything.

00:03:13.243 --> 00:03:15.297
I planned everything from a CEO level

00:03:15.297 --> 00:03:17.991
and then I did all the
work from a janitor level.

00:03:17.991 --> 00:03:19.021
And as I built it up to the point

00:03:19.021 --> 00:03:20.101
where I started making some money,

00:03:20.101 --> 00:03:21.848
I started handing off some of those tasks.

00:03:21.848 --> 00:03:24.673
And that let me go from a video a week,

00:03:24.673 --> 00:03:26.069
to a video a day.

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:28.322
And I moved closer and closer
and closer up the chain

00:03:28.322 --> 00:03:30.050
to the point where now
I'm guiding everything,

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.863
I'm still the on camera talent.

00:03:32.863 --> 00:03:35.183
Right, I still do this
work 'cause I love it.

00:03:35.183 --> 00:03:37.702
Not only because I'm good
at it and getting better,

00:03:37.702 --> 00:03:38.753
but I love it.

00:03:38.753 --> 00:03:40.247
This is what I love doing.

00:03:40.247 --> 00:03:42.480
I still review every video that goes out

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:43.845
and all the research behind it,

00:03:43.845 --> 00:03:46.252
'cause I love it, 'cause I learn from it.

00:03:46.252 --> 00:03:48.598
'cause I care about the
product that we're creating.

00:03:48.598 --> 00:03:50.770
But my team puts all that together.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:51.927
You know, even this.

00:03:51.927 --> 00:03:55.666
We use Evernote, oh let me load it up.

00:03:55.666 --> 00:03:57.024
You know, I use Evernote here

00:03:57.024 --> 00:03:58.506
and I got a list of all the topics

00:03:58.506 --> 00:03:59.699
I need to talk about today.

00:03:59.699 --> 00:04:01.359
All the topics, who I'm
doing shout outs for,

00:04:01.359 --> 00:04:03.167
where the research is, what the clips is

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:04.396
that I need to watch.

00:04:04.396 --> 00:04:06.004
All of that stuff, my
team puts together for me.

00:04:06.004 --> 00:04:07.562
This thing gets filmed,

00:04:07.562 --> 00:04:10.069
I have Jason behind the
camera filming it for me.

00:04:10.069 --> 00:04:12.015
He's going to send it to
Christine, my video editor.

00:04:12.015 --> 00:04:14.355
We've got three editors who
are going to cut it all up,

00:04:14.355 --> 00:04:15.953
post to the YouTube channel, title it,

00:04:15.953 --> 00:04:18.754
descriptions, tags, playlists,

00:04:18.754 --> 00:04:20.222
all of that stuff that goes up.

00:04:20.222 --> 00:04:22.237
And I'm guiding it from a high level.

00:04:22.237 --> 00:04:23.884
But I built it up to that point.

00:04:23.884 --> 00:04:26.156
If I was just starting out

00:04:26.156 --> 00:04:27.906
and that was my idea.

00:04:28.863 --> 00:04:30.276
Like, I'm going to do this

00:04:30.276 --> 00:04:32.649
and I'm going to wait for other
people to do things for me,

00:04:32.649 --> 00:04:33.880
it's not going to happen.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.337
And so it's thinking big,
I love it, think big,

00:04:36.337 --> 00:04:39.518
you need it, 'cause a lot of
people don't think big enough

00:04:39.518 --> 00:04:42.788
and they stay stuck being a
janitor for their entire life.

00:04:42.788 --> 00:04:45.538
Think big, it's great, but start.

00:04:47.115 --> 00:04:48.760
Be the janitor too

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.196
and work your way up.

00:04:50.196 --> 00:04:53.532
Add more value, focus on what
you can add the most value to,

00:04:53.532 --> 00:04:56.294
so you can bring on people to alleviate

00:04:56.294 --> 00:04:57.648
some of the tasks for you

00:04:57.648 --> 00:05:00.480
and help you build closer to
that big thing you want to do.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.698
To achieve your goal, you need
to think big and act small.

